      "role": "user",
      "content": "that works. i like the idea of using physical traits to show that they just don't play by the same rules as the empire. \n\nfor their culture, could you go deeper into their mindset? i want them to feel almost fundamentally different from the \"enlightened\" people. instead of law and logic, how would their social structure or way of thinking work? i want to lean into that sense that they are driven more by instinct or some kind of dark, primitive impulse rather than actual reason. what would their leadership or social order look like if it was based on that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
